{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794176866,"nonce":"Y9F5Uad/BgVwSBGJuJhryN1aa5s=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-e90c710-integration` (b84edc1..6b19657).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/done.rs: new lib module. resolve_base (explicit, then baseBranch, then origin/HEAD, then main/trunk/master/develop). async find (git log over \u003cbase\u003e and origin/\u003cbase\u003e, Refs trailer prefix match, no fetch). ready_epics and EpicCandidate. 14 tests (temp repos plus unit).\n- src/lib.rs: exports done.\n- src/app.rs: DoneSheet state, OpenDone, DoneFound, ToggleDone, PickDone, RunDone and DismissDone messages. Closes go through the per-repo write queue. Bugs close first, then epics. An epic is skipped with \"child X did not close\" if a child failed. Results are recorded per row. 8 new tests.\n- src/ui/done.rs: new modal sheet. Loading state, checkbox row per candidate with commits, All/None, Close selected, per-row Closing/Closed/Failed.\n- src/ui/screen.rs: \"Roadmap Done\" button on each git-bug repo card (disabled until issues load). Sheet overlay on the Repositories page.\n- src/ui/mod.rs: registers the done module.\n- src/theme/style.rs: scrim style for the modal backdrop.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 3 findings — 2 auto, 1 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- Dismissal (X, Esc, scrim, Done button) is blocked while the sheet is Closing, so planned epic closes are not silently dropped. Dropping the repo from the workspace still clears the sheet.\n- An epic qualifies only if it has at least one child and every child is closed or ticked. This matches the plugin's readyEpics. An epic's tick is inert while any child is unticked.\n- A row whose issue already has a write in flight fails at once (\"another write on this issue is in flight\") instead of waiting for a result that never arrives.\n- \"--\" added to git log so a base branch name that collides with a worktree path does not break it.\n- Not run visually: the UI was verified by compile, clippy and update-loop tests only, not by launching the app.","files":null}]}